WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.800
Raj: The out-of-band console works. Old kernel entry is present. Host A is ready to drain.

2
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:13.824
Lukas: Does your account have reboot access there? A visible console isn't the whole check.

3
00:00:13.824 --> 00:00:20.951
Raj: Yes, permissions are verified. I won't test a reboot outside the approved sequence.

4
00:00:20.951 --> 00:00:27.959
Priya: Just to confirm, active requests must finish first, right? No abrupt service stop.

5
00:00:27.959 --> 00:00:34.895
Hannah: Traffic is removed. I'm watching active connections and the other hosts' latency.

6
00:00:34.895 --> 00:00:41.231
Anika: I'll keep an eye on background jobs too. They don't show up as incoming connections.

7
00:00:41.231 --> 00:00:46.247
Lukas: Good. Confirm those are idle before stopping the app and rebooting.

8
00:00:46.247 --> 00:00:53.374
Raj: I'm on it. Jobs are idle now. What's the ETA for the final connection check?

9
00:00:53.374 --> 00:01:00.766
Hannah: Done. No active requests. Let's keep it under observation when it comes back.

10
00:01:00.766 --> 00:01:07.270
Priya: Okay, proceed with A only. Call out the boot result before restoring traffic.

